    "title": "Davie man charged with speeding, fleeing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n7 hours ago\nMARATHON — A 22-year-old Davie motorist was arrested on Tuesday, Sept. 30, for allegedly driving approximately 110 mph on U.S. 1 and fleeing from deputies.\nSyed Mohammad Qasim Hamdani was charged with DUI, fleeing and eluding, reckless driving, speeding more than 50 mph above the posted limit and resisting arrest, according to the Monroe County Sheriff's Office.\nDepuites were notified at 11 p.m. of a Kia sedan speeding and driving recklessly in Marathon. The vehicle was observed near mile marker 55 and stopped. The driver, Qasim Hamdani, smelled of alcohol, reports say. He then sped away from the traffic stop, reaching speeds of approximately 110 mph before the Kia’s tires were spiked and the Qasim Hamdani was taken in custody near U.S. 1 and 62nd Street, reports say.\n1",
